{:edb/db-before-t 2318 :edb/db-after-t 2319 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535631 50 #inst "2026-10-09T04:03:36.752Z" 13194139535631 true] [17592186229106 1020 #edb/ref 17592186358377 13194139535631 true] [17592186229106 1020 #edb/ref 17592186358384 13194139535631 true] [17592186229107 1020 #edb/ref 17592186358391 13194139535631 true] [17592186229107 1020 #edb/ref 17592186358395 13194139535631 true] [17592186229482 1017 #edb/ref 17592186227515 13194139535631 false] [17592186229482 1017 #edb/ref 17592186358371 13194139535631 true] [17592186229482 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535631 true] [17592186229482 1100 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nUsing the implicit Euler method with step size $Δx=0.25,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step.\nWhich of the following is the **general form** of $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ in terms of the new values ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ and the current value $y?$" 13194139535631 true] [17592186229482 1100 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$y^{′} = x^{2} - y^{2}, y(0) = 1$\nUsing the implicit Euler method with step size $Δx = 0.25$, the new value $y_{new}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g(y_{new}) = 0$ at each step.\nWhich of the following is the **general form** of $g(y_{new})$ in terms of the new values $x_{new}$ and $y_{new}$, and the current value $y$?" 13194139535631 false] [17592186229482 1145 "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2})\\cdot 0.25 \\\\  & =0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and move all terms to the left-hand side and define the resulting expression as $g({y}_{\\text{new}}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2} \\\\ {{0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}}_{⏟}}_{g({y}_{\\text{new}})} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=0.25$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}.\n$$" 13194139535631 true] [17592186358371 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358372 13194139535631 true] [17592186358371 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358373 13194139535631 true] [17592186358371 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358374 13194139535631 true] [17592186358371 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358375 13194139535631 true] [17592186358371 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358376 13194139535631 true] [17592186358371 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535631 true] [17592186358371 1041 "selection" 13194139535631 true] [17592186358371 1104 #edb/ref 17592186358372 13194139535631 true] [17592186358371 1110 #uuid "6d9ee173-a796-55ff-b6c6-51ac496eba73" 13194139535631 true] [17592186358372 1034 "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}" 13194139535631 true] [17592186358372 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535631 true] [17592186358372 1111 #uuid "04a38549-e9d0-5292-b347-f74fdc9a6a15" 13194139535631 true] [17592186358373 1034 "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}+y-0.25{y}^{2}" 13194139535631 true] [17592186358373 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535631 true] [17592186358373 1111 #uuid "9a7e7195-94cf-5506-a52a-8100b8c7530e" 13194139535631 true] [17592186358374 1034 "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25{y}^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}" 13194139535631 true] [1759